   "text": "Across both compounds, the computed descriptor profiles fall within ranges generally regarded as drug-like, with no Lipinski violations and ring, polarity, and lipophilicity values consistent with orally dosed small molecules. The drug-likeness scoring and synthetic accessibility estimates suggest reasonably favorable and synthetically tractable profiles, though the presence of structural alerts for one of the compounds warrants follow-up on potential reactive or promiscuous substructures rather than dismissal. The solubility and CNS-relevant composite predictions are in-silico proxies only, and the panel-pass tally reflects computational heuristics rather than experimental developability data. None of these results establish efficacy, safety, or clinical relevance for either compound; they support only a preliminary physicochemical and rule-based triage, and should be followed by orthogonal computational checks and experimental validation before any further inference is drawn.\n\n*This paragraph is LLM reasoning over the findings above. It is tagged HYPOTHESIS: it contains no numbers of its own and was itself checked against the claims ledger before publication.*",
